      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-126826",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $r(t)=7\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\,i+24\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nn=\\frac{a(t)\\,i+b(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{\u2032}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $b(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14052255/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "5309709b1ea193a28f9093382172180b60526c0aaf567e20b12a422b0af2078f"
